tests: state the rollback depth rule in test-recurrent-state-rollback
Fold-into: hexagon-spec/0002-llama-bound-the-recurrent-rollback-by-the-last-ubatch.patch

The defect

The test rolls back past the tokens of the last ubatch of a sequence at two places:
test_rollback rolls back 3 tokens after three decodes of one token each, and
test_multi_seq_split_replay rolls back all the tokens of a tail ubatch of 3 tokens. The slot
groups that such a rollback reads hold the states of an earlier ubatch. The test passes without
the depth bound of seq_rm only because its replay decodes the same tokens as that earlier ubatch,
thus the old groups hold the correct states by chance. With the depth bound, seq_rm refuses the
two rollbacks, and the test stops at "partial rollback failed" and at "multi-seq prefill/rollback
failed".

The change

At the two places, the test asserts that seq_rm refuses the rollback, with a comment that gives
the rule: a rollback may not go deeper than the tokens of the last ubatch of the sequence. Then
test_rollback clears the sequence, decodes the prompt again as one ubatch and rolls back inside
it, and test_multi_seq_split_replay decodes the sequence again with a last ubatch that starts one
token before the rollback point. The partial checkpoint and the split replay then cover a pending
rollback (rs_idx != 0), as the test intends. The reference context of the split replay keeps its
one prefill ubatch.

Base: llama.cpp commit c6824a9 with the patches of patches/series above this one.

